---
Meta: zensim workspace zensim--feature-v2e, phase-5 strip-tiled v2 pipeline
(bandwidth-hypothesis test, STRIP_ROWS=128). Parent commit 7696b62a (phase-4
landing).
Command: cargo build -p zensim --features training,feature-regime-v2 --bench v2_speed_baseline --release
         ./target/release/deps/v2_speed_baseline-<hash>   (full sweep, no --group filter)
Bench config: min_rounds=15, max_time=30s per group (phase-3's widened config, unchanged).
Host: same shared workstation as phases 3/4, load-gated before launch (1-min
load 0.13 at launch time, well under the efficiency ladder's 8.0 gate
threshold; load rose to ~8 by the time this sweep finished due to unrelated
leftover wait-loop processes from this same session, cleaned up afterward —
did not affect this run, which had already completed).
No -C target-cpu=native.

Pre-sweep signal (2048²-only, 3-point STRIP_ROWS selection, same load-gating,
not itself part of this file): STRIP_ROWS=32 -> 2.71x, STRIP_ROWS=64 -> 2.39x,
STRIP_ROWS=128 -> 2.31x. STRIP_ROWS=128 selected as the value for this sweep.

GATE RESULT (1024x1024, 1-thread): v1=64.9ms, v2=147.0ms, ratio=2.27x.
GATE (<=1.5x): NOT MET. Down from phase-4's 3.09x (a 26.5% relative ratio
reduction at the gate size), but does not close the gate.

Kill criterion (phase-5 addendum): "strip-tiling improves 2048x2048 by <20%
=> bandwidth hypothesis falsified". Measured: v2 871.9ms (phase-4, no strip)
-> 650.8ms (phase-5, strip-tiled) = 25.4% reduction. NOT TRIGGERED -- the
bandwidth hypothesis is CONFIRMED: memory traffic from full-image
intermediate planes was a real, measurable ~25-30% component of phase-4's
size-dependent slope. The ratio did not reach the pre-registered "~1.2-1.8x
compute floor" (landed at 2.31x @ 2048x2048 instead), meaning bandwidth was
A dominant term, not the only one -- see docs/FEATURE_V2_SPEC_2026-07-18.md
SS A.15.6 for the updated residual attribution (dense-block division count
is now the clearer larger remaining share).

Side finding: 256x256 REGRESSED under strip-tiling (1.18x phase-4 -> 1.50x
phase-5), exactly the diagnostic the efficiency ladder pre-registered ("if
256sq gets slower, strip overhead is too high"). Fixed per-strip halo-gather
cost (HALO_P=10 rows, paid on every strip regardless of size) outweighs the
memory-traffic saving at small images that already fit cache under the
phase-4 (non-strip) design. See SS A.15.4 for the full reasoning.
